==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Wolf Princess Deale''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Jester Queen Deale''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Deale can be a useful midranger/supporter to deal with bulky [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]]/[[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] enemies with few knockbacks, particularly [[Angelic Sleipnir]], since Sleipnir is not only tanky, but he can also use his knockback ability to push slowly, something that Deale's [[Knockback|Knockback]] can counter. Thanks to her multi-hit ability, she has a very high chance to knockback Angel/Alien enemies, which can help in case you get cornered.

However, in case you're fighting fast, strong pushers like [[Angelic Gory]] or [[Teacher Bun Bun]], always bring bulky cats (against Angels, it's recommended to bring [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]]) to protect her, as her knockbacks may fail and give you trouble. Using her against these won't do much though, as they'll gain the ground they pushed to very quickly, making the knockback do nearly nothing other than adding a chance of leading hitters to miss.

==='''True Form'''===
Getting the True Form is pretty cheap, and only gives Deale one change: she now has zero time between attacks, essentially attacking nonstop. This wouldn't be much, but now she has almost '''7.5k''' damage per second. This makes Deale one of the better general damage units in the game. You will have to be wary of her Knockback, and should avoid bringing her to any Alien/Angel stages with nasty backline supports. While she loses prominence later into SOL and UL with most generalists, she can still be a great choice should no specialist work.

==='''Talents'''===
Jester Queen Deale's first talent is an improvement to her existing Knockback ability, raising it from 40% to a maximum of 60%. This makes her Knockback ability far more reliable and is recommended for situations where missing a knockback or two would be dangerous. However, even at 60%, Deale's Knockbacks are far from consistent.

Her talents give her two immunities: '''[[Immune to Waves|Wave Immunity]]''' and '''[[Immune to Weaken|Weaken Immunity]]'''. Wave Immunity is particularly useful against general wave stages, especially with [[Youcan]], [[Bun Bun Symbiote]], and [[Elizabeth the LVIth]] in her target traits. Weaken Immunity, while not as useful, can still see some use due to her DPS and range. Realistically, this matters most against [[Calamary]] and [[Cli-One]], both of whom outrange Deale and can be troublesome with their Weaken. [[Winged Pigge]] is also an enemy that becomes a lot easier with this talent, as her Omni Strikes can get quite annoying. However, aside from them, this Talent is not that useful since she can outrange most Weakening enemies or just needs to knock them back with or without the damage.

Finally, she gets the standard '''Attack Buff''' and '''HP Buff''' talents. As a stat-based unit, and especially as a ranged attacker, these can be rather useful. Her DPS is high enough with her range to make the Attack Buff talent work, should you intend on using her for her offenses. Defense Buff is not as useful, as she does use her long range and 5 knockbacks, but it doesn't hurt.

==='''Ultra Talents'''===
The first Ultra Talent Deale gets is a guaranteed '''[[Wave Attack|Mini-Wave]]''' on each hit. This Talent allows her to Knockback enemies really far away, and occasionally results in a double Knockback if enemies are far enough away from her. [[Colossus Slayer]] has many notable matchups, which make it an excellent addition: [[Archangel Exiel]] and [[Super Hyppoh]] are both fast and hard-hitting enemies that can push very easily, and with Deale, they can be controlled easier. She's even good in [[Baron Seal Strikes]], being able to push away all of Baron Seal's support at least once and can deal solid damage to the seal itself. Lastly, '''[[Immune to Curse|Curse Immunity]]''' is pretty situational, as Angel enemies are seen with relic enemies a lot, but Alien isn't as common. It isn't recommended to get this talent. This talent can go well in [[Gigahaniwan Strikes!]] as if you got her Wave immune talent then she can be safe from Gigahaniwan and knockback the Gokurakko far from your units without getting cursed.

Overall, investing in Deale's Ultra talents isn't a bad idea. By getting her to level 60 you're also boosting her pretty solid damage even higher, and Colossus Slayer further adds to that, along with Mini-Wave too.

